The manual is a workbook for the development of professional hygiene and hygiene training skills. It offers information on:
- the importance of using training programs that focus on environmental issues;
- how to develop skills that help reduce the risk of health and safety issues from infection;
- how to increase the effectiveness of a health and hygiene programme;
- how to apply best practice approaches to a health and hygiene policy;
- how to develop standards of hygiene that will support training and policies.
All the information contained in the manual is intended to be used by health workers or their employers; however, it should not be used by health workers for the purpose of assessing the effectiveness of such programmes.
